    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today's slate with a clear directive: capitalize on favorable right-handed matchups to bolster our standing in the 5x5 categories. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (82.13) headlines the lineup, serving as our strongest play due to an ideal combination of a high-leverage leadoff spot and a soft matchup against Feltner (xERA 4.69). His elite sprint speed makes him the primary engine for our stolen base aggression today, further boosted by a massive 17% SP Skill bump. Similarly, **Christian Yelich** (73.18) and **Kyle Schwarber** (68.21) provide elite production profiles; **Christian Yelich** benefits significantly from the dynamic platoon advantage against Cecconi, while **Kyle Schwarber** continues to demonstrate high-end efficiency with a strong 0.388 xwOBA, proving that his power profile is well-aligned for tonight\u2019s conditions.\n\nOn the bench, **Jacob Gonzalez** (50.78) was the most difficult exclusion, narrowly missing the cut behind the superior efficiency of **Casey Schmitt** (56.25). While **Jacob Gonzalez** carries solid base projection value, the optimizer prioritized the 11% platoon edge that **Casey Schmitt** draws against Holmes. We are also managing a \"Below Floor\" situation with **Dillon Dingler** (33.99), whose 19% negative SP Skill adjustment against Brown rendered him a bench stash to protect our game caps. Risk management remains centered on **Yordan Alvarez**; despite his elite 0.452 xwOBA, he faces the toughest individual matchup of our starters against Valdez, leading to a calculated 9% platoon penalty that lowers his overall output. Monitor these spots closely, as the scarcity of stolen bases makes the production from **Pete Crow-Armstrong** and **Christian Yelich** the absolute priority for tonight\u2019s rotation.",
